  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the grill to high. Finely chop the onion. Slice the tomato. Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick slices, then pat dry with paper towel. Put 1½ tsp Moroccan seasoning in a shallow dish. Turn the haloumi in the seasoning to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/289806/photos/large/prep_ingredients-5324016a2f01dc8aba4ef5f9d6c53e45.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make apricot relish: Heat 2 tsp olive oil in a small frypan over medium heat. Cook the onion, stirring, for 3-4 mins until softened. Add the remaining Moroccan seasoning and season with salt and pepper. Add the apricots, 2 tsp white wine vinegar and 2 tsp sugar and cook, stirring occasionally, for 1-2 mins until thickened. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/289807/photos/large/make_apricot_relish-90286161cb6719fa2b2ca818625e05d7.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pan-fry haloumi: Meanwhile, heat 2 tsp olive oil in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the haloumi for 1-2 mins each side until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/289808/photos/large/pan_fry_haloumi-e5134a17de660aa21c275048f3a26b8b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast buns: Cut the buns in half. Put on an oven tray, cut side up, and grill for 3 mins or until lightly toasted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/289809/photos/large/toast_buns-dfd840e92c622b7bd2c8da4c8443749e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Spread the bun bases with 2 tbs mayonnaise. Top with the tomato, rocket, haloumi and apricot relish. Sandwich with the bun tops and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/289810/photos/large/serve_up-22e0656a8dfaed1db205c599627eed29.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Want fries with that? For a healthier side of spuds, preheat the oven to 220C. Scrub potatoes or sweet potatoes, then cut into wedges, toss in olive oil and salt, and roast for 20-25 mins until golden.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/289811/photos/large/make_it_yours-2db2ff71b7182b1a7d70a0bca5f13d96.jpeg"
    }
  ]
